From: Stability Audit <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:04:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] fix(cloud): scope onChange restore-guard to the hydrating
 tab; allow saving emptied cloud diagrams

- onChange was dropped for every tab whenever ?cloudDiagramId= was in the URL
  and the cloud scene flag was false, which starves local tabs of selection,
  dock, minimap, autosave and snapshot persistence. Guard now keys off the id
  of the tab actually being hydrated (cloudRestoringTabIdRef).
- Deleting all elements of an existing cloud diagram threw 'canvas is empty'
  in autosave and in switchCanvasTab. Pass allowEmpty via allowsEmptyCloudSave()
  (tombstones count as a real edit); new-diagram creation still refuses empty.
- switchCanvasTab skips the cloud flush when the scene has no element records.

Tests: tests/stability-onchange-and-empty-save.test.js (6). Full suite: no new
failures vs baseline (86 pre-existing failures unchanged).
